<tool id="rameau" name="Rameau" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="20.01">
    <description>Analysis and processing of hydrogeological data</description>
    <macros>
        <token name="@TOOL_VERSION@">1.2.0</token>
        <token name="@VERSION_SUFFIX@">0</token>
    </macros>
    <requirements>
        <container type="docker">brgmcode/rameau:@TOOL_VERSION@</container>
    </requirements>

    <command detect_errors="exit_code">
        /app/entrypoint.sh
    </command>

    <configfiles>
        <inputs name="inputs" filename="inputs.json" data_style="paths"/>
        <configfile name="outputs" filename="outputs.json"><![CDATA[{
            "output": "$output",
            "outputs_dir": "outputs"
        }]]></configfile>
    </configfiles>

    <inputs>
        <param name="run" type="select" value="Forecast" optional="false" multiple="true" label="Execution mode">
            <option value="Forecast">Forecast</option>
        </param>
        <section name="param_section" title="Configuration files" >
            <param name="param" type="data" format="toml" label="Configuration file"/>
            <param name="arbros" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Connectivity file"/>
        </section>
        <section name="data_section" title="Data files" >
            <param name="etp" type="data" format="csv" label="Potential evapotranspiration"/>
            <param name="pluie" type="data" format="csv" optional="false" label="Rainfall"/>
            <param name="debit" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Discharge"/>
            <param name="piezo" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Piezometric level"/>
            <param name="temperature" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Temperature"/>
            <param name="neige" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Snow"/>
            <param name="pre_surf" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Surface water abstractions"/>
            <param name="pre_sout" type="data" format="csv" optional="true" label="Groundwater abstractions"/>
        </section>
    </inputs>    
 
    <outputs>
        <data name="output" format="toml" label="Result" />
        <collection name="outputs" type="list" label="Results">
            <discover_datasets pattern="__designation_and_ext__" directory="outputs"/>
        </collection>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <param name="run" value="Forecast"/>
            <section name="param_section">
                <param name="param" value="params.toml" ftype="toml"/>
                <param name="arbros" value="arbros.csv" ftype="csv"/>
            </section>
            <section name="data_section">
                <param name="etp" value="etp.csv" ftype="csv"/>
                <param name="pluie" value="pluie.csv" ftype="csv"/>
                <param name="debit" value="debit.csv" ftype="csv"/>
                <param name="piezo" value="piezo.csv" ftype="csv"/>
            </section>
            <output name="output" ftype="toml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="[files]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="outputs" type="list" count="2">
                <element name="forecast_riverflow" ftype="csv">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_text text="member,norain"/>
                        <has_text text="Watershed 1"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
                <element name="forecast_watertable" ftype="csv">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_text text="member,norain"/>
                        <has_text text="Watershed 1"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
            </output_collection>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[
RAMEAU
======

This tool performs lumped and semi-distributed hydrogeological modelling with **RAMEAU**.

One execution mode is available:

- **forecast**: to produce ensemble forecasts from an already calibrated model

If several modes are selected, the optimisation is run first.

Required parameters and files
=============================

Configuration files
-------------------

- **Configuration file (TOML)**: Required regardless of the execution mode.
- **Connectivity file (CSV)**: Required **only** if the TOML file defines several catchments (multi-catchment or semi-distributed modelling).

Data files
----------

All CSV files must be **tab-separated**.

- **PET**: Required. Potential evapotranspiration time series (mm).
- **Rainfall**: Required. Precipitation time series (mm).
- **Discharge**: Required for **rainfall-discharge** or **rainfall-discharge-level** models. Data in m³/s.
- **Piezometric level**: Required for **rainfall-level** or **rainfall-discharge-level** models. Data in m.
- **Temperature**: Required if the **snow module** is used. Data in °C.
- **Snow**: Required if the **snow module** is used. Snowfall data in mm.
- **Surface water abstractions**: Required if the influence of **river abstractions** is modelled.
- **Groundwater abstractions**: Required if the influence of **aquifer abstractions** is modelled.

Output files
------------

The files produced depend on the **execution mode** and the **model type**.

- A **simulated discharge time series** is produced for rainfall-discharge and rainfall-discharge-level models.
- A **simulated piezometric time series** is produced for rainfall-level and rainfall-discharge-level models.
- A TOML file containing the **optimised parameters** is generated for **optimisation** and **forecast**.
- A **performance metrics** file is generated for **optimisation** and **simulation**.
]]></help>
